  "description": "ENOYUC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H112 Ce3 Mn5 N1 O37. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 17 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.746-4.225 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.05-154.91°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H112Ce3Mn5NO37. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 7 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV), Mn(IV), Mn(III).",
